To send a proposal request to a user's WalletConnect session using a Node.js backend server, you'll need to use the WalletConnect library. Here's a step-by-step guide:

1. First, install the WalletConnect library in your project:

```bash
npm install --save @walletconnect/web3-provider @walletconnect/modal
```

2. Import the necessary modules in your server file:

```javascript
const WalletConnectProvider = require("@walletconnect/web3-provider").default;
const WalletConnectModal = require("@walletconnect/modal").default;
```

3. Initialize WalletConnectModal:

```javascript
const walletConnectModal = new WalletConnectModal({
  projectId: "your_project_id", // replace with your project id from WalletConnect
  metadata: {
    name: "Your App Name",
    description: "Your App Description",
    url: "https://yourapp.com",
    icons: ["https://yourapp.com/icon.png"],
  },
});
```

4. Create a WalletConnectProvider instance:

```javascript
const provider = new WalletConnectProvider({
  infuraId: "your_infura_id", // replace with your Infura ID
  bridge: "https://bridge.walletconnect.org",
});
```

5. Connect to the user's wallet:

```javascript
async function connect() {
  try {
    await provider.enable();
    console.log("Connected to WalletConnect!");
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Failed to connect to WalletConnect:", error);
  }
}
```

6. Send a proposal request:

```javascript
async function sendProposal() {
  try {
    const session = await provider.sendCustomRequest({
      method: "eth_sendTransaction",
      params: [
        {
          from: "user_address", // replace with the user's address
          to: "contract_address", // replace with the contract address
          value: "0x00",
          gas: "0x76c0",
          gasPrice: "0x9184e72a000",
          data: "0xd46e8dd67c5d32be8d46e8dd67c5d32be8058bb8eb970870f072445675058bb8eb970870f072445675",
        },
      ],
    });
    console.log("Proposal sent:", session);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Failed to send proposal:", error);
  }
}
```

7. Finally, call the `connect` and `sendProposal` functions:

```javascript
(async () => {
  await connect();
  await sendProposal();
})();
```
